1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:26,880
it has been evident for some time now that this day had to come it was unavoidable

2
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:31,160
i'm sure that some of you may have already heard the news

3
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:37,360
but for the rest of you the moriartes face a crisis as yet unprecedented

4
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:49,320
so i hope you're ready for this lads it'll take all of our expertise to achieve a decisive victory

5
00:00:49,320 --> 00:01:02,760
sorry i'm late have you already all for one and one for all right wait come again

6
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:29,520
i can't pull the street at night

7
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:33,520
行き詰まる君の視線に

8
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:36,520
i feel your sickness in your eyes

9
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:40,520
傷ついて壊していこう

10
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:44,520
終わりなきこのpunishment

11
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,520
i feel your sins

12
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:48,520
いつでも

13
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:52,520
抜かれられない take me away

14
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:56,520
i don't feel your love but i can give you love

15
00:01:56,520 --> 00:02:00,520
目が覚めるような夢を見せてよ

16
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:04,520
i don't feel your love but i can give you love

17
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:08,520
目が覚めるたび君は崩れる

18
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,520
いつか

19
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:26,520
抜かれられる

20
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:29,520
見つけ出して

21
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,520
美容 heart

22
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:36,500
A tea party?

23
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:37,680
Yes.

24
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:40,640
As I'm sure you're aware,

25
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:44,420
tea parties are held by each household on a rotating basis.

26
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:47,360
I've had great success over the years,

27
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:49,780
politely declining the opportunity to host.

28
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,960
But the Earl of Rockwell recently founded in himself

29
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,740
to take me to task over it.

30
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:00,080
So it is with great reluctance, I must say,

31
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:02,480
it is finally time that our household

32
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:04,640
fulfill that particular duty as well.

33
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:09,220
He's really not making an effort to disguise

34
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:11,740
how much he truly hates this, is he?

35
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:14,880
We only have until this Sunday to prepare.

36
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,880
What major obstacles do we face?

37
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,600
I was just getting to that.

38
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,380
As you may recall,

39
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,940
there was once a few amongst the noble ladies

40
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:26,020
who had the temerity to sidle up to will,

41
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:29,260
under pretense of viewing a prize-winning rose garden.

42
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:32,960
I imagine we will see the same such ladies once again.

43
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,460
Those who view this merely as an opportunity

44
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:37,080
to approach men of stature.

45
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,180
I bet.

46
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:41,660
But that means you're in just as much danger as he is, aren't you?

47
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,160
Indeed.

48
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:46,400
Ordinarily, Will and I are more than capable of handling such situations.

49
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,120
However,

50
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:53,720
these women become quite unpredictable when they let their hair down,

51
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:56,820
and are emboldened even further in greater numbers.

52
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:00,220
It is this group psychology that is the issue.

53
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:02,660
We'll be overrun,

54
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:04,400
and then there is the house.

55
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:07,140
We have the operations room in the cellar,

56
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,400
and a collection of many other items

57
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:12,240
which must be kept private at any and all costs.

58
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:19,740
The challenge is to direct this tea party to a successful end,

59
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:22,000
free from any snooping noble eyes.

60
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,300
A battle not easily fought.

61
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,580
We'll have nearly a hundred guests here.

62
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:30,340
Far more than we'll be able to handle on our own.

63
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:33,520
We have no choice but to hire some temporary help.

64
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:35,640
Then obviously overseeing that help

65
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:37,580
is going to be necessary to plan for as well.

66
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:38,920
Dear brother,

67
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:41,440
might I ask you to supervise them?

68
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:42,800
I suppose so.

69
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:46,480
Understand that I can only give this particular role

70
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:48,100
to the person I trust the most.

71
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,580
Very well, then.

72
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,620
As long as I can be of help to you.

73
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,200
Perfect.

74
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:57,440
I'm afraid we won't be able to invite Patterson

75
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,840
due to his work obligations.

76
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:00,920
But Fred,

77
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,040
do reach out to Herder, won't you?

78
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:06,380
I believe I've just started the perfect post to assign him.

79
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:07,520
Sure.

80
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:08,640
I can do that.

81
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:10,020
All right.

82
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:14,500
Our task is to play ideal employees of an Earl's household

83
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:18,100
and send our guests home in good spirits with good stories.

84
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:19,120
Understood?

85
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:20,420
Right!

86
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,060
Hmm.

87
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,340
Ah, what perfect weather.

88
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:37,560
I've rallied the troops.

89
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:38,540
Right.

90
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,800
Now, let's review our charges one last time.

91
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,320
Once Albert concludes his remarks,

92
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:48,480
I will oversee our guests as they dine in the main venue.

93
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:52,200
I will supervise our temporary kitchen employees,

94
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:55,000
thus keeping my focus inside the estate.

95
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,560
And our set position will be right here in the garden.

96
00:05:58,560 --> 00:05:59,980
Indeed, it will.

97
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:03,080
Well, we'll keep our eyes open and assist each other as needed.

98
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:06,240
I'm here primarily as bodyguard for you two.

99
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:07,560
As for me,

100
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:10,160
I'll entertain any guests who visit the Rose Garden.

101
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,800
And I will be here flitting about the grounds

102
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:15,540
until such a time that someone calls upon my expertise.

103
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:16,460
Correct.

104
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,620
You will be our hit-and-run attacker.

105
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:22,840
Your skills provide a sort of insurance against the unexpected.

106
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:26,020
We are marching into war, after all.

107
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:27,880
Well, that's a bit frightening.

108
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,200
Wait, did Hodor ever show himself?

109
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:31,500
Ah.

110
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:35,380
He's already on standby at his designated location.

111
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:36,580
Ah.

112
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,580
My word.

113
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:41,240
Here I thought I'd been invited to a tea party,

114
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:44,740
and then I find out that I'm stuck in charge of these dingy quarters.

115
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,400
What do I have to do?

116
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:50,160
You'd think William would trust me a bit more at this point.

117
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:54,120
But he did say that I could do as I please down here,

118
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:55,980
as long as I listened carefully.

119
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:00,920
So I think I'll work on these delightful puzzle rings he gave me.

120
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:02,820
Ooh.

121
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:06,260
If I rotate this one like this...

122
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:15,460
To battle.

123
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:30,600
I've given up hope that this day would ever arise.

124
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:33,220
This is the Moriarty Estate Tea Party we've all been pining for.

125
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:36,180
And this is darling Albert and his middle brother William weren't enough on their own.

126
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,840
I've heard that even their servants have been looking.

127
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:38,320
Oh my.

128
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:40,320
They both fight the Enchanting Garden, don't they?

129
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,120
Come now, girls.

130
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:43,540
If we let this chance get away, we'll never get another one.

131
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:47,380
You're crazy now, love.

132
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:48,840
No need to get in front of me.

133
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:49,540
I'm not.

134
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,500
You're just crazy.

135
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,460
We have to sit as close as possible.

136
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,580
Then hurry up before the Ellens get ahead of us.

137
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,000
Hello, ladies.

138
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,420
We are honored by your presence here today.

139
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:05,220
They're beyond beautiful.

140
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:09,420
As you enter the grounds, please sign in at reception.

141
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:11,700
And there's no need to run.

142
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:19,780
As a result, please direct your gratitude to the Earl of Rockwell.

143
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:23,640
For it's thanks to him alone that we have welcomed you all here today.

144
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,880
I'm sure you're well aware, but we're quite a bashful bunch.

145
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:32,800
Despite all appearances, my brother William and I are nervous simply standing before you.

146
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:39,300
Now, we do hope you will avail yourselves of this opportunity to stop by our family's rose garden.

147
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:45,860
Our gardener has been hard at work, and we are pleased to see his roses have bloomed just in time to welcome you.

148
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:50,280
And we have plenty of snacks prepared for you as well.

149
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:53,360
Stay in chat for as long as time permits.

150
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:57,360
The second these remarks are over, I'm making a beeline straight for Albert.

151
00:08:57,680 --> 00:09:00,780
And the moment he so dares to let go of his cup, I'm off to William!

152
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,180
These strong girls!

153
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:08,400
Without further ado, a toast to your health and to a most splendid day.

154
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:31,340
This pressure is intense.

155
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,080
Should I step in already?

156
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:36,420
He looks all right, but is he really?

157
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:42,720
I have been looking forward to conversing with all of you.

158
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:48,260
But with each of you talking over each other, I can't give you the attention you deserve.

159
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:53,360
I was under the impression that tea parties were a much more elegant affair.

160
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:56,520
An environment in which one can create bonds.

161
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:58,100
Share secrets.

162
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:00,940
Wouldn't that be nicer?

163
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:11,260
We have more than enough time, so please, do allow me to speak to you one by one.

164
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:14,260
Yes, the gentleman does make a very good point.

165
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:15,400
He does indeed.

166
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:18,800
I can scarce remember why we were in such a hurry in the first place.

167
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:21,360
Impressive work, Albert.

168
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:23,500
Pardon us.

169
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:26,540
We thought we'd go and have a look at the rose garden.

170
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:29,960
If you're not otherwise occupied, perhaps you'd like to join us?

171
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,960
I'm afraid I must decline.

172
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:35,520
My apologies, but I'm unable to leave my post here.

173
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,160
Oh, what a shame.

174
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:38,640
Another time.

175
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:41,360
Those broad shoulders.

176
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:43,260
Good luck in there, Fred.

177
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,100
Excuse me, Fred.

178
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,760
What sort of roses are these fluffy ones here?

179
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:55,840
Ah, yes.

180
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:58,580
They're a type of bourbon rose called boule de neige.

181
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:03,440
All bourbon roses have this shape, but these are cultivated for their color.

182
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,260
Their name means snowball.

183
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,720
I've never seen anything like them.

184
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:10,160
Are you the one who grew these gorgeous things?

185
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:12,920
I am.

186
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:14,820
And I'm glad you enjoy them.

187
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:15,740
Truly.

188
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:17,360
I'm flattered.

189
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:34,220
My roses.

190
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:42,760
I hope you're all right.

191
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,800
Those thorns can be nasty.

192
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:47,220
Oh, Fred.

193
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,420
Please, I assure you, I'm quite well.

194
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:50,620
See to your roses.

195
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,400
No, the roses are merely an addition.

196
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:56,220
An embellishment here to highlight your beauty.

197
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:01,000
And as such, I cannot allow them to bring harm to any of you.

198
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:02,360
Oh!

199
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:04,820
How dashing!

200
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:14,160
Much of the fervor outside has passed, so please make sure we have no shortage of snacks or tea as our guests find their calm.

201
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:15,620
Sir.

202
00:12:15,620 --> 00:12:23,800
I'm terribly sorry, but I stumbled on my way out to the garden, and I shattered this lovely teapot.

203
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:26,660
You needn't spend your worries on a teapot.

204
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:29,240
Tell me, you're not hurt, are you?

205
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:30,680
I'm fine, sir.

206
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:34,400
And which guest had this been brewed for, my dear fellow?

207
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:37,560
Oh, it's... this was for the young master, William.

208
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:38,420
For brother.

209
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:41,360
Oh, then let's make him a fresh pot.

210
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,080
We will let it steep a bit longer.

211
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:08,220
Brother likes it strong, after all.

212
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:15,620
Now, then, if you would like to make the delivery, my friend, it should be just the right temperature by the time you pour it.

213
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,360
Yes, sir!

214
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:21,660
Oh, my! How's heaven there?

215
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:30,960
No! You wouldn't really go that far, would you?

216
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,900
Just imagine if anyone found out.

217
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,800
I'll worry about that if the time comes.

218
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:38,860
One must dig one's claws in, else no one will ever get any closer to them.

219
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:39,940
I suppose.

220
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:43,640
Dear lady, what's the rush?

221
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:44,900
I beg your pardon, ma'am.

222
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:51,020
Where on earth could she have gone?

223
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:51,040
Where on earth could she have gone?

224
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:57,040
Where on earth could she have gone?

225
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:13,400
All right, honey.

226
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:23,380
Things are proceeding smoothly enough.

227
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,820
I only hope that we can keep it up.

228
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:29,620
And on that note, how is William doing?

229
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:33,560
Simply keep that in mind and it shan't give you any trouble.

230
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:37,640
Wow. I never would have conceived of such a thing if not for you.

231
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,180
You have my gratitude.

232
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:40,680
Oh, William.

233
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:44,620
William, could I trouble you to advise me on my concern next?

234
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:45,560
But of course.

235
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:50,020
I'm afraid mine is a matter of the heart.

236
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:53,460
You see, there is a man whom I simply adore at the moment.

237
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:57,080
But I haven't the foggiest idea as to how to approach him.

238
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,240
All right.

239
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:02,080
Would you perchance be willing to tell me a bit more about this person?

240
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:03,600
Yes, indeed.

241
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:06,440
He's a mathematician and the younger brother of an earl.

242
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:09,780
And though I regrettably don't know him half as well as I would like,

243
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:11,960
I'm certain he is deeply kind.

244
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:17,360
Whenever I so much as think of this gentleman, my poor heart aches.

245
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,840
And naturally, I saw a doctor.

246
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:24,760
But he insisted that only William James Moriarty could possibly cure what hails me.

247
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:27,020
I grow more concerned by the hour.

248
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:31,140
They do say that lovesickness can be quite deadly, do they not?

249
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:33,260
Uh, yes.

250
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,220
I'm sure they do.

251
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,040
This ain't my circus, mate.

252
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:44,660
You're on your own.

253
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:47,360
Good luck, William.

254
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:49,040
Hmm?

255
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,280
Uh, I can't help you either.

256
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:58,920
An intruder in William's room.

257
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:00,600
Bond.

258
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:07,280
Oh, pardon me.

259
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:08,540
I must answer a call.

260
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,140
Oh, do come back.

261
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:15,480
I really think we should get out of here.

262
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:16,500
Oh, no.

263
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:20,220
I have to burn this room into my memories before I so much as think about leaving.

264
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:21,880
Look at all of this.

265
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:24,680
So many difficult-looking mathematics books.

266
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:28,860
By the looks of things, I suppose William really does spend most of his time in the study.

267
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:30,020
Oh?

268
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:31,320
What is this?

269
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:38,660
Oh, goodness.

270
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:40,900
They're as pretty as a painting.

271
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:43,520
How sublime they all are.

272
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:46,360
Look.

273
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:50,080
This must be William's walking stick.

274
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,500
Wait, perhaps we ought not.

275
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:55,160
Oh, my.

276
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:56,220
Look at this.

277
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:57,940
It's put together like a scabbit.

278
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:00,240
Ah!

279
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:03,160
Gracious.

280
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:04,580
That was silly.

281
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:06,880
So it was a magic wand all along.

282
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:11,700
I can't imagine why he'd keep a childish thing like this lying around.

283
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:12,820
My, my.

284
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:18,460
What naughty little kittens you must be to wander into a place such as this uninvited.

285
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:21,060
Now, why don't we return to the party?

286
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:23,900
Yes!

287
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:26,420
He is as handsome as all the rest!

288
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,700
May I ask you for your name?

289
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:29,440
Hush now.

290
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:30,880
You didn't even want to be here.

291
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:31,540
Ladies, please.

292
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:32,300
Let me have this one.

293
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:34,220
There's more than enough of me to go around.

294
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:34,660
I can't see.

295
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:39,540
We anticipated that someone would try to sneak into our rooms, and now I'm glad we did.

296
00:17:40,060 --> 00:17:41,500
It's all set dressing up there.

297
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:43,360
There's nothing of any great import.

298
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:44,260
Could then.

299
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:47,500
But the one place that we really can't afford to be seen.

300
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:52,120
I don't know how she could have possibly made her way down here.

301
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:55,460
But she is quite the little explorer, so...

302
00:17:55,460 --> 00:18:02,280
Someone's coming.

303
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:12,820
Albert was crystal clear that if, by some slim chance, anyone were to stumble upon this operations room, then I am authorized to neutralize them.

304
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:16,080
Regardless of who they are.

305
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:18,740
Where does this lead?

306
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:19,740
Where does this lead?

307
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:28,080
A wine cellar?

308
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:35,540
Oh, hello.

309
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:37,500
And who might you be?

310
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:41,180
If I may be honest, I was expecting a biped.

311
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,880
So let's have a look around, then, you and I.

312
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,920
This is awful.

313
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:48,140
Where in the world could she have gotten off to?

314
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:53,100
Is this who you were looking for?

315
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:54,660
Yes, it is.

316
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:56,920
Oh, dear, I thought I lost you.

317
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:59,800
You have my thanks, but may I ask who you are?

318
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:02,720
I am one of William's most prized employees.

319
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:05,560
A problem solver of the highest intellect.

320
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:09,560
Whenever he has a problem that deludes him, I am the one he calls upon.

321
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:10,700
I see.

322
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:12,320
And what's this?

323
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:12,960
That.

324
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:16,460
That is a leash that will extend up to 30 yards.

325
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:20,840
It seemed a perfect fit for this curious little girl, so you're more than welcome to keep it.

326
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:21,520
Truly?

327
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:22,980
How wonderful!

328
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:24,700
Thank you ever so much!

329
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:25,880
Of course.

330
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,880
But we should head back to the garden now.

331
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:29,880
Please, allow me to show you the way.

332
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:38,500
My word, what a perfectly charming way to spend an afternoon.

333
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:40,900
It was most enjoyable.

334
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,260
Thank you, gentlemen.

335
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:45,740
I'm so pleased to hear that you all had a good time.

336
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,840
We'll see you again soon.

337
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:58,200
I've just realized, I don't believe I saw Lewis Moriarty at all today.

338
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:00,740
Yes, I so wanted to speak with him.

339
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:02,660
Or at least see his face.

340
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,280
Perhaps next time.

341
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:05,520
Next time, indeed.

342
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:09,980
Nice work, brother.

343
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:14,160
And keeping Lewis away from the front lines was precisely the right decision.

344
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:15,160
Thank you.

345
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:15,700
Thank you.

346
00:20:15,700 --> 00:20:17,480
It was an easy call.

347
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:20,240
We can't have the boy attracting unwanted lady friends.

348
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:24,320
Our temporary hires have been compensated and dismissed.

349
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:25,580
So mission accomplished?

350
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:28,060
Mission accomplished.

351
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:29,280
Thank you, Lewis.

352
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,660
You must be tired.

353
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:32,880
Please feel free to take the evening off.

354
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:35,520
Right.

355
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:44,000
Hey, Patterson.

356
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,940
We got our money's worth today.

357
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:47,800
Good.

358
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:50,780
From the state of things, it looks like it was quite the ordeal.

359
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:53,140
Where are William and the old man?

360
00:20:53,660 --> 00:20:55,480
I believe they've already retired.

361
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:56,860
Albert has gone too.

362
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:58,260
Is that right?

363
00:20:58,660 --> 00:20:59,580
That's a shame.

364
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:02,660
Then who on earth will I share this with?

365
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:04,600
You shouldn't have.

366
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:08,920
I declined an invitation from Lestrade because I wanted to come here instead.

367
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:11,480
So I'm going to indulge either way.

368
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:12,420
Join me?

369
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:23,980
I do have to say, I hope you didn't do anything untoward to the ladies at the tea party.

370
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,780
I wouldn't have had the time.

371
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:28,040
I was busy fulfilling my duties.

372
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:31,200
I don't believe it.

373
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:34,440
It almost sounds as though you've finally discovered the joy of labor.

374
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:40,460
Though I do feel like I've forgotten about something.

375
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:53,180
I wonder when their little tea party will be over.

376
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:57,900
I do still have plenty of these charming ring puzzles William gave me.

377
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:01,380
So I could spend an eternity down here if I so wished.

378
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:05,100
But surely they haven't all forgotten about me.

379
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:06,720
That would be ridiculous.

380
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:28,260
It could spend time with half an hour when they get on my head.

381
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:38,500
I feel lost, I feel lost

382
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:43,860
書きのくった手紙のことだけは覚えてない

383
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:45,940
It's so true, it's so true

384
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:52,180
気にすって私を恨まないで

385
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:57,780
2つに届けて 手のひらで踊る

386
00:22:57,780 --> 00:23:02,660
代償にも一度 与えられるだろう

387
00:23:02,660 --> 00:23:10,900
広いと風になる 午前後時

388
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:17,400
思い出を二人戻そう 最後の日に

389
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:25,500
美しさ望むなら迷うなと

390
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:31,380
罪を拭い去るように 終わらせて

